    <string name="shadow_note_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="shadow_note_body">Shadow privilege never changes the process uid. The process stays an ordinary user; credentials are elevated only for the duration of the single system call that actually needs them, then reverted immediately.\n\nThe kernel stores no allowlist. The decision is based on a 32-byte token at 0x1000000000 in the process own memory. The token is derived from the uid, so the same uid always yields the same value.\n\nThe manager should therefore read the token and inject it into the target process — never let the target read it by itself, or any app could authorize itself.</string>
