    <string name="um_intro_title">What is UM</string>
    <string name="um_intro_body" formatted="false">In short: make one specific app unable to see a specific file, while every other app and the system still see it normally.

Unlike a normal module (which puts files on disk and needs a reboot), UM changes nothing on disk and needs no reboot - it only affects the permission check at that moment.</string>
    <string name="um_intro_more" formatted="false">How to use ▾</string>
    <string name="um_intro_full" formatted="false">[Can do]
· hide a chosen file from one chosen app
· only that app is affected
· rules are stored encrypted and loaded at boot

[Cannot do]
· cannot change app internals (that is LSPosed)
· cannot replace system files (that is a normal module)
· currently only the "hide file" action

[Rule format]
one rule per line: uid N dev N ino N
example: uid 10560 dev 65082 ino 1073146 hide

Get dev and ino with: stat -c "%%d %%i" &lt;path&gt;

[Import]
1. write the line in any text editor, save as .txt
2. tap "Import UM module" below
3. the app validates and encrypts it
4. tap it in the list to apply
</string>
